cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "scrna-cellstate-similarity: transcriptional similarity between annotated cell states across single-cell RNA-seq datasets"
abstract: >-
  R pipeline that quantifies the transcriptional similarity between cell
  states annotated in two single-cell RNA-seq datasets, typically a human
  reference atlas and a mouse model, using three complementary readouts:
  elastic-net logistic regression, Spearman correlation of z-scored
  pseudobulk profiles, and SingleR label transfer, on a shared 1:1 ortholog
  gene universe with symmetric renormalisation.
authors:
  - family-names: "Andres Ejarque"
    given-names: "Rosa"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0012-1155"
    affiliation: "King's College London"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-16"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/r-andrese/scrna-cellstate-similarity"
keywords:
  - single-cell RNA-seq
  - cell-state annotation
  - cross-species comparison
  - mouse models
  - SingleR
  - R
